{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Did I not say to you, do not sin against the child?</b> For he did not intend to bring about your death when he did what he did as you thought — rather, his deeds, inasmuch as he was a child, were not directed toward a purposed end." "<b>And also his blood, behold, it is required.</b> The sin now called to account is not the cruelty alone, as you thought, but also his blood — for you sinned in seeking to shed innocent blood, of one who was not worthy of death as you thought; and behold, without doubt he died in his servitude."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:34:20.327141946Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}